# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitignore — MDT-TS-and-Scripts
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This repository contains the scripts, task sequences, configuration files,
# and documentation for an MDT deployment share. The large binary content
# (operating system images, driver packs, update packages, application
# installers, boot images) lives in the companion OneDrive folder and on
# network shares — NOT in Git.
#
# The rules below enforce that separation. If you find yourself needing to
# commit a file that this file ignores, please read CONTRIBUTING.md and
# open a Discussion first — do not silently weaken these rules.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. MDT RUNTIME ARTIFACTS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are created by MDT during a deployment. They must never be
# committed because they contain machine-specific state and can be very
# large. They are also cleaned up by CleanupScripts.ps1 at the end of a
# successful deployment.

_SMSTaskSequence/
MININT/
LTIBootstrap.vbs
LiteTouch.lnk

# MDT-generated log files (deployment logs, task sequence logs, etc.)
*.log
!docs/**/*.log.example

# MDT deployment summary and monitoring data
BDD.log
BDD_*.log
SMSTS.log
SMSTS*.log
ZTIGather.log
ZTIDiskpart.log
ZTIApplications.log
ZTIDrivers.log
ZTIPatches.log
ZTIBackup.log
ZTIConfigure.log
ZTIDomainJoin.log
ZTIGroups.log
ZTIUserState.log
ZTIBIOSCheck.log
ZTINextPhase.log


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. CREDENTIALS AND SECRETS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bootstrap.ini stores credentials in PLAINTEXT. Never commit a real
# Bootstrap.ini. Commit Bootstrap.ini.example (or similar) with placeholder
# values, and instruct users in the README to copy it and fill in their own.

Control/Bootstrap.ini
Control/Bootstrap.ini.*
!Control/Bootstrap.ini.example
!Control/Bootstrap.ini.template

# CustomSettings.ini is tracked, but if you add a machine-specific
# override or a local credentials file, ignore it here.
Control/CustomSettings.local.ini
Control/*.local.ini

# Task sequence specific rules files that might contain credentials
Task Sequences/**/Rules.bootstrap.ini
Task Sequences/**/Rules.local.ini

# Any .env files (in case future tooling uses them)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generic secrets
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
credentials.json


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. OPERATING SYSTEM IMAGES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WIM, ESD, VHD, VHDX files are multiple gigabytes each. They live in the
# companion OneDrive folder, not in Git. The XML metadata files
# (OperatingSystems.xml, OperatingSystemGroups.xml) that describe them ARE
# tracked.

*.wim
*.esd
*.vhd
*.vhdx
*.vmdk
*.vdi
*.avhdx

# But keep the small XML metadata files that describe them
!Operating Systems/*.xml
!OperatingSystems.xml
!OperatingSystemGroups.xml

# Ignore everything under the OS source folders except the XML metadata
Operating Systems/**/*
!Operating Systems/*.xml


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. BOOT IMAGES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LiteTouchPE_x64.wim and LiteTouchPE_x86.wim are ~500 MB each and are
# regenerated locally by "Update Deployment Share". They live on the
# companion OneDrive folder for users who want a pre-built copy.

Boot/*.wim
Boot/*.iso
Boot/*.esd

# Keep the boot folder structure documented via .gitkeep if needed
!Boot/.gitkeep


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. OUT-OF-BOX DRIVERS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MDT driver folders contain thousands of small .inf/.sys/.cat/.dll files
# adding up to many gigabytes. The metadata file Drivers.xml and
# DriverGroups.xml ARE tracked (they describe which drivers are imported),
# but the actual driver binaries live on the companion OneDrive folder or
# on a network share.

Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.inf
Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.sys
Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.cat
Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.dll
Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.exe
Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.bin
Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.cab
Out-of-box Drivers/**/*.msi

# Keep the group/metadata XML files at the root of the Out-of-box Drivers folder
!Out-of-box Drivers/Drivers.xml
!Out-of-box Drivers/DriverGroups.xml


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. UPDATE PACKAGES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Windows cumulative updates, .msu files, and .cab packages are hundreds of
# megabytes each. They are copied into the offline image at deploy time.
# The Updates folder structure is tracked via a .gitkeep placeholder.

Updates/**/*.msu
Updates/**/*.cab
Updates/**/*.psf
Updates/**/*.xml.tmp

!Updates/.gitkeep
!Updates/**/.gitkeep
!Updates/README.md


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. APPLICATION INSTALLERS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MSI, EXE, MSIX, APPX installers are large binaries. The Application
# metadata (Applications.xml, ApplicationGroups.xml) that MDT uses to
# reference them IS tracked, but the actual installers live in the
# companion OneDrive folder or on a network share.

Applications/**/*.msi
Applications/**/*.exe
Applications/**/*.msix
Applications/**/*.msixbundle
Applications/**/*.appx
Applications/**/*.appxbundle
Applications/**/*.msp

!Applications/Applications.xml
!Applications/ApplicationGroups.xml
!Applications/README.md

# Packages (MDT packages) — same rule
Packages/**/*.msi
Packages/**/*.exe
Packages/**/*.cab

!Packages/Packages.xml
!Packages/PackageGroups.xml
!Packages/README.md


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. ARCHIVE FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Split 7-Zip archives (Apps.7z.001, Drivers.7z.002, LGPO.7z, etc.) are
# downloaded at runtime by the payload updater scripts from the companion
# repositories. They must never be committed.

*.7z
*.7z.001
*.7z.002
*.7z.003
*.7z.004
*.7z.005
*.7z.006
*.7z.007
*.7z.008
*.7z.009
*.7z.010
*.rar
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz

# Exception: small documentation samples if you ever add them
!docs/examples/*.zip


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 9. PAYLOAD HASH FILES AND LOCAL STATE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The payload updaters write .sha256 files and download staging content
# to these locations on the target machine. They should never be
# committed to the repo even if you run the scripts locally.

*.sha256
C:/Temp/OEM/
C:/Recovery/OEM/Logs/
C:/ProgramData/OEM/Logs/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 10. PREREQUISITES — INSTALLERS AND ARCHIVES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Prerequisites folder contains configs (tracked) and some installers
# or self-extracting archives (not tracked). Keep the configs, ignore
# the large binaries.

Prerequisites/**/*.exe
Prerequisites/**/*.msi
Prerequisites/**/*.msu
Prerequisites/**/*.cab
Prerequisites/**/*.7z
Prerequisites/**/*.zip
Prerequisites/**/*.iso
Prerequisites/**/*.wim

# Keep the small config files
!Prerequisites/**/*.xml
!Prerequisites/**/*.cmd
!Prerequisites/**/*.ps1
!Prerequisites/**/*.ini
!Prerequisites/**/*.md


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 11. TASK SEQUENCE RUNTIME STATE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The task sequence definitions themselves (ts.xml, Unattend.xml) ARE
# tracked. But some MDT tools create backup or state files alongside them
# during editing, which should not be committed.

Task Sequences/**/*.bak
Task Sequences/**/*.old
Task Sequences/**/*.orig
Task Sequences/**/*.tmp
Task Sequences/**/~$*


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 12. WINDOWS OPERATING SYSTEM JUNK
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files that Windows creates automatically when you browse a folder.
# These should never be committed.

Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
*.url
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 13. TEMPORARY AND BACKUP FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# General temp files, swap files, and backups.

*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.old
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*.swo
*~
~$*
*.crdownload
*.partial
*.part


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 14. EDITOR AND IDE FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Settings and workspace files from common editors. Users can still keep
# their own local settings — they just won't be tracked in the repo.

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json.example
!.vscode/launch.json.example
!.vscode/extensions.json

.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Sublime Text
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# JetBrains Rider / VS Code workspace
*.code-workspace


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 15. POWERSHELL ARTIFACTS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files generated by PowerShell tooling (PSScriptAnalyzer, Pester, etc.)

*.ps1xml
PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1.local
TestResults.xml
*.Tests.ps1.bak
CodeCoverage.xml

# PowerShell module cache
**/Modules/**/*.psd1.local


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 16. GIT INTERNAL FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Files that Git itself can create during normal use.

.gitattributes.bak
.gitmodules.bak
*.orig.git
*.orig.gitignore


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 17. REPOSITORY-SPECIFIC EXCEPTIONS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This section is for files that would normally be caught by a broad rule
# above, but that we WANT to commit because they are part of the project.

# Documentation assets (small images, diagrams, screenshots)
!docs/images/*.png
!docs/images/*.jpg
!docs/images/*.jpeg
!docs/images/*.gif
!docs/images/*.svg

# Small placeholder scripts and samples inside docs
!docs/examples/*.ps1
!docs/examples/*.cmd
!docs/examples/*.wsf
!docs/examples/*.xml
!docs/examples/*.ini
!docs/examples/*.md

# Activation scripts (small, non-sensitive .cmd files)
!$OEM$/$1/Recovery/OEM/Activation/*.cmd
!$OEM$/$1/Recovery/OEM/Activation/*.ps1

# Small XML definition files used by the OEM\Update scheduled task
!$OEM$/$1/Recovery/OEM/Apps/Update.xml

# LGPO tool — if the tool is committed as a small .exe (LGPO.exe) under
# $OEM$, keep it. Otherwise rely on LGPO.ps1 to download it.
!$OEM$/$1/Recovery/OEM/LGPO/LGPO.exe
!$OEM$/$1/Recovery/OEM/LGPO/*.txt

# .gitkeep placeholder files keep empty directory structures
!.gitkeep
!**/.gitkeep


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# END OF .gitignore
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# If you need to force-add a file that this file ignores, use:
#   git add -f <file>
# and please explain WHY in your commit message and PR description.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
